WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.529
Chips and Cheese

00:00:01.565 --> 00:00:03.321
Qualcomm's Oryon 3

00:00:03.145 --> 00:00:04.147
reaches the top

00:00:04.662 --> 00:00:06.053
Chester Lam's deep

00:00:05.865 --> 00:00:06.713
dive into the

00:00:06.525 --> 00:00:08.034
third-generation Oryon

00:00:07.846 --> 00:00:08.671
cores in the

00:00:08.483 --> 00:00:10.263
Snapdragon X2 Elite

00:00:10.487 --> 00:00:11.843
whose P-cores deliver

00:00:11.655 --> 00:00:13.246
CPU performance that

00:00:13.058 --> 00:00:14.379
challenges the best

00:00:14.261 --> 00:00:16.996
x86-64 chips and

00:00:16.832 --> 00:00:18.211
outnumber the E-cores

00:00:18.035 --> 00:00:18.871
two to one

00:00:19.390 --> 00:00:20.793
From Oryon 1

00:00:20.911 --> 00:00:22.338
Oryon 3 inherits

00:00:22.185 --> 00:00:23.458
an out-of-order window

00:00:23.305 --> 00:00:24.342
in excess of

00:00:24.154 --> 00:00:25.793
600 micro-ops

00:00:26.318 --> 00:00:27.815
Oryon 3 increases

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:28.511
core width to

00:00:28.323 --> 00:00:29.525
9 micro-ops

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:30.398
up from 8

00:00:30.209 --> 00:00:31.376
in its predecessor

00:00:31.518 --> 00:00:32.096
and makes a

00:00:31.908 --> 00:00:33.134
number of improvements

00:00:32.945 --> 00:00:34.195
throughout the pipeline

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:35.748
Full story on

00:00:35.559 --> 00:00:36.455
the dashboard
